{{<layout}}{{$body}}
<h1>Programs</h1>
{{#flash}}{{^secret}}{{#good}}<p class="done">{{text}}</p>{{/good}}{{#bad}}<p class="problem">{{text}}</p>{{/bad}}{{/secret}}{{/flash}}

{{#newToken}}
<div class="card">
  <p class="meta"><strong>Copy this now.</strong> It is shown once and never again &mdash; what this
    server keeps is a hash of it, so nobody here can read it back to you, including us.</p>
  <pre class="token"><code>{{.}}</code></pre>
  <p class="hint">Paste it into whatever asked for it. If you lose it, revoke the token below and
    make another; that is cheaper than a token nobody can account for.</p>
</div>
{{/newToken}}

{{#wasAsked}}
<div class="card">
  <h2>Authorize <em>{{asking}}</em>?</h2>
  <p>It is asking for a token that can do whatever <strong>you</strong> can do here, and nothing
    more. {{#expires}}It will stop working in {{tokenDays}} days.{{/expires}}
    {{^expires}}It does not expire; revoke it when you are done with it.{{/expires}}</p>
  {{#atLimit}}<p class="problem">You already have {{maxTokens}} token(s), which is as many as this
    community allows. Revoke one below first.</p>{{/atLimit}}
  {{^atLimit}}<form method="post" action="{{action}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="authorize">
    <input type="hidden" name="name" value="{{asking}}">
    <button type="submit">Authorize {{asking}}</button>
  </form>{{/atLimit}}
</div>
{{/wasAsked}}

<p class="hint">A token lets a program act as you &mdash; a command line tool that pushes this
  site's pages from a folder on your machine, a script that keeps them in a git repository. It can
  do exactly what you can do here and never anything more, and everything it does is recorded as
  <em>you</em>, because a community has to be able to ask who put something here and get somebody
  they can talk to.</p>

<h2>Your tokens</h2>
{{^anyTokens}}<p class="hint">None yet.</p>{{/anyTokens}}
{{#anyTokens}}
<div class="scroller"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>what</th><th>made</th><th>last used</th><th>expires</th><th></th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#tokens}}<tr>
    <td>{{label}}</td>
    <td class="dim">{{made}}</td>
    <td class="dim">{{#used}}{{.}}{{/used}}{{^used}}never{{/used}}</td>
    <td class="dim">{{#forever}}never{{/forever}}{{^forever}}{{expires}}{{/forever}}</td>
    <td class="actions"><form class="inline" method="post" action="{{action}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="action" value="revoke">
      <input type="hidden" name="token" value="{{id}}">
      <button type="submit" class="quiet">Revoke</button>
    </form></td>
  </tr>{{/tokens}}</tbody>
</table></div>
{{/anyTokens}}

{{^wasAsked}}
<h2>Make one</h2>
{{#atLimit}}<p class="hint">You have {{maxTokens}}, which is the most this community allows. Revoke
  one above to make another &mdash; rotating the oldest away for you would stop whatever is using
  it, and you would find out from something breaking.</p>{{/atLimit}}
{{^atLimit}}<form method="post" action="{{action}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="action" value="authorize">
  <div><label for="t-name">what is it for</label>
    <input id="t-name" type="text" name="name" maxlength="40" placeholder="my laptop" required></div>
  <div class="doing"><button type="submit">Make a token</button></div>
</form>{{/atLimit}}
{{/wasAsked}}

<h2>Using it</h2>
<p class="hint">Send it as a bearer token. Every answer is JSON, and every refusal says why in a
  sentence rather than a status code alone.</p>
<pre><code>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" {{base}}/whoami

# what this site holds, as one file
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" {{base}}/content &gt; site.json

# what would change, without changing it
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" --data-binary @site.json "{{base}}/content?dry=1"

# and for real -- only what differs is written, and the answer says what moved
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" --data-binary @site.json {{base}}/content</code></pre>
{{^canWriteContent}}<p class="hint">Reading and writing this community's pages needs permission you
  do not have yet, so a token of yours can hold this site's calendar open and little else for
  now.</p>{{/canWriteContent}}
<p class="hint"><a href="{{selfUrl}}">&larr; back to your page</a></p>
{{/body}}{{/layout}}
